{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Not</b> — The reason: HaShem put the force of soul in man, and placed in his hand the living creatures and plants, to recognize the deed of HaShem and to praise Him while he is yet alive." "<b>Those who go down to silence</b> — A place of cutting off and a land of decree, like ודמיתי אמך (Ezekiel 16:44). And some say: it is from the root of ולא דמיה לי, and do not vocalize it with a dagesh in the mem — and how much less so given that after it is written —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 115, :notes {1 "The phrase 'do not vocalize it with a dagesh in the mem' (אל תתני דמי לו) involves a wordplay on דומה/דמי that is difficult to render; the instruction concerns whether the mem of דומה carries a dagesh. The trailing 'כתוב -' appears to introduce a quotation that the comment cuts off without completing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:47.869896969Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}